# Git Workflow

- **Default integration branch:** `staging` (day-to-day commits). CI runs on
  `staging` and `main`.
- **`main`:** protected production branch — update only via PR from `staging`
  (or a focused fix branch). Merge that PR with a **merge commit**, not squash
  or rebase, so `staging` and `main` keep a shared history.
- After `main` updates, workflow `sync-staging.yml` merges `main` back into
  `staging` (or opens a PR if it conflicts). Do not leave the branches diverged.
- Purpose-based short-lived branches are fine; merge into `staging` first when possible.
- Commit only when asked. Messages explain why.
- Never commit secrets.
- Small, reviewable diffs. Include summary, test plan, and docs when architecture or business rules change.
- Product releases: bump versions on `staging`, open PR → `main`, then tag `v*` (on the merged main commit preferred) to run Product Release.
